[agent:bash] databricks tables create --help
[agent:result] command: databricks tables create --help
[agent:result] stdout: This command is in Public Preview and may change without notice.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] Create a table.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   Creates a new table in the specified catalog and schema.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   To create an external delta table, the caller must have the
[agent:result]   **EXTERNAL_USE_SCHEMA** privilege on the parent schema and the
[agent:result]   **EXTERNAL_USE_LOCATION** privilege on the external location. These privileges
[agent:result]   must always be granted explicitly, and cannot be inherited through ownership
[agent:result]   or **ALL_PRIVILEGES**.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   Standard UC permissions needed to create tables still apply: **USE_CATALOG**
[agent:result]   on the parent catalog (or ownership of the parent catalog), **CREATE_TABLE**
[agent:result]   and **USE_SCHEMA** on the parent schema (or ownership of the parent schema),
[agent:result]   and **CREATE_EXTERNAL_TABLE** on external location.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   The **columns** field needs to be in a Spark compatible format, so we
[agent:result]   recommend you use Spark to create these tables. The API itself does not
[agent:result]   validate the correctness of the column spec. If the spec is not Spark
[agent:result]   compatible, the tables may not be readable by Databricks Runtime.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   NOTE: The Create Table API for external clients only supports creating
[agent:result]   **external delta tables**. The values shown in the respective enums are all
[agent:result]   values supported by Databricks, however for this specific Create Table API,
[agent:result]   only **table_type** **EXTERNAL** and **data_source_format** **DELTA** are
[agent:result]   supported. Additionally, column masks are not supported when creating tables
[agent:result]   through this API.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   Arguments:
[agent:result]     NAME: Name of table, relative to parent schema.
[agent:result]     CATALOG_NAME: Name of parent catalog.
[agent:result]     SCHEMA_NAME: Name of parent schema relative to its parent catalog.
[agent:result]     TABLE_TYPE:
[agent:result]       Supported values: [
[agent:result]         EXTERNAL,
[agent:result]         EXTERNAL_SHALLOW_CLONE,
[agent:result]         FOREIGN,
[agent:result]         MANAGED,
[agent:result]         MANAGED_SHALLOW_CLONE,
[agent:result]         MATERIALIZED_VIEW,
[agent:result]         METRIC_VIEW,
[agent:result]         STREAMING_TABLE,
[agent:result]         VIEW,
[agent:result]       ]
[agent:result]     DATA_SOURCE_FORMAT:
[agent:result]       Supported values: [
[agent:result]         AVRO,
[agent:result]         BIGQUERY_FORMAT,
[agent:result]         CSV,
[agent:result]         DATABRICKS_FORMAT,
[agent:result]         DATABRICKS_ROW_STORE_FORMAT,
[agent:result]         DELTA,
[agent:result]         DELTASHARING,
[agent:result]         DELTA_UNIFORM_HUDI,
[agent:result]         DELTA_UNIFORM_ICEBERG,
[agent:result]         HIVE,
[agent:result]         ICEBERG,
[agent:result]         JSON,
[agent:result]         MONGODB_FORMAT,
[agent:result]         MYSQL_FORMAT,
[agent:result]         NETSUITE_FORMAT,
[agent:result]         ORACLE_FORMAT,
[agent:result]         ORC,
[agent:result]         PARQUET,
[agent:result]         POSTGRESQL_FORMAT,
[agent:result]         REDSHIFT_FORMAT,
[agent:result]         SALESFORCE_DATA_CLOUD_FORMAT,
[agent:result]         SALESFORCE_FORMAT,
[agent:result]         SNOWFLAKE_FORMAT,
[agent:result]         SQLDW_FORMAT,
[agent:result]         SQLSERVER_FORMAT,
[agent:result]         TERADATA_FORMAT,
[agent:result]         TEXT,
[agent:result]         UNITY_CATALOG,
[agent:result]         VECTOR_INDEX_FORMAT,
[agent:result]         WORKDAY_RAAS_FORMAT,
[agent:result]       ]
[agent:result]     STORAGE_LOCATION: Storage root URL for table (for **MANAGED**, **EXTERNAL** tables).
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] Usage:
